# Not used (see meta.json, classification: excluded). This region's entry
# point is test_embedded_metadata_describes_the_transformation(tmp_path:
# Path) -- it does not take a graph as input at all. It writes an input
# project file, shells out to the project's own CLI to produce a
# cardinality.ttl, and only then parses *that* into the graph it reads
# assertions against. A single static fixture.ttl parsed up front (the
# generic oracle:values contract this file was scaffolded for) cannot stand
# in for output the region's own subprocess call is responsible for
# producing. driver.py calls the region directly with a real tmp_path
# instead of fixture=; see driver.py and meta.json for the actual (and
# irreducible) blocker.
@prefix ex: <http://example.org/> .
